      "description": "Current-program time progress paired with a readable time label.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-airing\"><span>3:00 PM – 3:30 PM</span><div class=\"ds-track\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span></span></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-airing{font:.8rem Roboto,system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-variant,#49454f);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-track{height:4px;border-radius:100px;margin-top:.5rem;background:var(--md-sys-color-secondary-container,#e8def8)}.ds-track span{display:block;width:50%;height:100%;border-radius:inherit;background:var(--md-sys-color-primary,#4f378b)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Material Broadcast",
    "overview": "This is an operating interface, not a streaming-service marketing page. Material Design 3 provides the consistent component language: readable workhorse typography, tonal surfaces, explicit selection states, and familiar touch-friendly controls. The viewer and administration share the same visual system.\n\nThe implementation uses Google's official Material Web filled/outlined buttons and icon buttons alongside native controls and Bootstrap layout/collapse utilities. `public/css/style.css` owns the shared tokens; `public/css/client.css` owns viewer-specific patterns. `frontend/material.js` selects the vendored component bundle. These files, rather than historical screenshots, are implementation authority.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Violet actions and lavender selection containers.",
      "Shared light/dark tonal surfaces.",
      "Compact, readable schedules and generous touch targets.",
      "Flat surfaces at rest; depth comes from tonal hierarchy."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Shared Theme Rule",
        "body": "Viewer and admin use one `theme` preference and the same semantic tokens; neither owns a separate palette. An unset preference follows the device.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The State Color Rule",
        "body": "Red means error or a destructive action. It is not a decorative accent.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tonal Depth Rule",
        "body": "Prefer a surface role over a new shadow or independent hardcoded background.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** pair every surface/container color with its corresponding foreground token.",
      "**Do** keep viewer and admin theme behavior identical.",
      "**Do** preserve readable text and at least 44px interactive targets on phones.",
      "**Do** keep schedule overflow inside the schedule region.",
      "**Do** preserve semantic states, keyboard operation, reduced motion, and visible focus."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** restore a separate dark-only viewer palette.",
      "**Don't** replace task controls with decorative streaming-service shelves.",
      "**Don't** use color alone to communicate an error, selection, or destructive action.",
      "**Don't** add decorative shadows to flat tonal containers."
    ]
  }
}
